# Python-generated files
__pycache__/
*.py[oc]
build/
dist/
wheels/
*.egg-info

# Virtual environments
.venv

# Local secrets
.env

# Personal working notes, kept local and purged from history (2026-09-06). No tracked
# file cites them: every reference was inlined or dropped on 2026-09-07, so a stranger
# with only the clone can still follow every claim. DECISIONS.md and INVENTORY.md stay
# tracked. Do not reintroduce a citation to any file listed below.
#   CLAUDE.local.md    the owner's working rules, renamed from CLAUDE.md on 2026-09-07.
#                      The tracked CLAUDE.md is now newcomer orientation instead.
#   DECISIONS.local.md the personal/process/housekeeping rows pruned out of DECISIONS.md
#                      on 2026-09-07; no tracked file cites any ID in it, by construction.
#   RUNBOOK.md         the GPU cluster procedure, untracked on 2026-09-07: it is specific
#                      to one university cluster and names its hosts.
#   research.md        the 2026-09-07 literature/forensics sweep. Findings, not decisions:
#                      anything it establishes graduates to DECISIONS.md with its own ID.
#   research_latency.md the 2026-09-11 rerank-latency literature sweep. Same rule: findings,
#                      not decisions -- anything adopted graduates to DECISIONS.md.
CLAUDE.local.md
spec.md
SESSION.md
DECISIONS.local.md
RUNBOOK.md
research.md
research_latency.md

# Per-machine Claude Code permissions. .claude/settings.json is deliberately NOT
# ignored -- it is the shared, committable half.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Regeneratable data (raw filings, parsed/chunked output) -- large,
# reproducible from scripts/pipeline/01_corpus.py.
# Keep: logs (*.jsonl) and day2_findings.md.
data/filings/
data/parsed/
data/chunks/

# Regeneratable HPC split-job payloads/outputs (embeddings, rerank scores) --
# large, reproducible via the split-job phases in scripts/pipeline (03_index, 05_arm3_rerank).
# Keep the small aggregated *_dev_results.json/*_dev_failures.md instead.
data/*_embed_payload.json
data/*_rerank_payload.json
data/embed_results.jsonl
data/rerank_scores*.jsonl
data/*_rerank_scores.jsonl

# CPU smoke-test output (n=5 sanity check before the real HPC run) -- not the
# recorded numbers, keep only the full *_dev_results.json/*_dev_failures.md.
data/*_cpu_dev_results.json
data/*_cpu_dev_failures.md

# Day 8 payloads: HPC round-trip inputs, rebuilt in minutes on the laptop from the
# scripts that made them. The *scores* they produced are kept (13.5 GPU-hours) --
# see the exceptions below, which override the *_rerank_payload rules above.
data/day8_*payload*.json

# Day 8 diagnostic dumps -- regeneratable free (no GPU, no API) from
# scripts/archive/failure_triage.py; 15MB of raw failure text.
data/day8_failure_cases.json
data/day8_failure_cases_retr16v2.json
data/day8_failure_slices/

# Superseded Day 8 outputs, kept ignored until deleted from disk:
#   day8_retr16_scores.jsonl        the RETR-22 run, taken on the variant-contaminated
#                                   pool; superseded by day8_retr16v2_dev_scores.jsonl
#   day8_slice_scores_t150.jsonl    old (unfiltered, raw-query) ordering; superseded by
#                                   the _filtered_stripped file per COST-17/COST-18
#   day8_cost13_smoke.jsonl         n=2 smoke test, not a recorded number
data/day8_retr16_scores.jsonl
data/day8_slice_scores_t150.jsonl
data/day8_cost13_smoke.jsonl

# Label audit (RETR-9/RETR-34) -- 38MB, all of it, deliberately including the verdicts.
# cases/ and blind/ replay from scripts/archive/label_audit_prepare.py (SEED=17; case_id
# hashes the question id, not the labels, so ids survive matcher changes). verdicts/ are
# model-generated, not human, and the audit is closed: its rates, mechanism and the
# RETR-35 cross-check are all written up in DECISIONS.md RETR-34/RETR-35. Re-running is
# an API cost, not a lost record. Score with label_audit_score.py before deleting on disk.
data/label_audit/*

# Batch API request payloads (COST-32). One JSONL per submitted job, regenerated
# deterministically from data/day8_cost13_payload.json + --thinking, so the file is a
# transport artifact rather than a record. What matters is kept: the *responses* land in
# the tracked day8_cost13_responses.jsonl, each row carrying its own tier and thinking
# level, and the job name is printed at submit time for --resume.
data/batch_jobs/

# RETR-7/RETR-8 re-index working files (INFRA-12)
data/retr7_rr_*_payload.json
data/retr7_rr_*_scores.jsonl
data/chunks_pre_retr7/
data/retr7_embed_payload.json
data/retr7_embed_results.jsonl
data/ingest_log.jsonl
.DS_Store
models/
# Resume state for the two ONNX/ORT archive probes -- partial progress, not records.
# The results they produce are the tracked onnx_parity_results.json and
# ort_fp32_latency.json. ort_fp32_partial/ was tracked by accident until 2026-09-07;
# its three files were byte-identical to the legs already inside ort_fp32_latency.json.
data/onnx_parity_partial/
data/ort_fp32_partial/

# --- Overrides: GPU/paid outputs the rules above wrongly swept up -----------------
# A rule that says "regeneratable" is wrong when regenerating costs GPU hours or money.
# These are records, not working files. ~39MB total.
#   retr7_rr_*_scores.jsonl        the RETR-39 headline's own rerank pass. Read by
#                                  ci_fixture_build.py, 07_arm6_loop.py, onnx_rerank_parity.py
#                                  -- i.e. CI-1, AGENT-16, AGENT-26, DEPLOY-9 all cite it.
#   day6_arm4_*_rerank_scores      three GPU passes (ARM4-10). A is still the live control.
#   rerank_scores.jsonl            the original Arm 3 GPU pass (ARM3-1..3).
#   day8_cost13_payload.json       COST-34 upgraded this to Keep; the day8_*payload* rule
#                                  above still ignored it. Changing it silently moves both
#                                  stored arms.
!data/retr7_rr_dev_scores.jsonl
!data/retr7_rr_test_scores.jsonl
!data/day6_arm4_A_rerank_scores.jsonl
!data/day6_arm4_B_rerank_scores.jsonl
!data/day6_arm4_C_rerank_scores.jsonl
!data/rerank_scores.jsonl
!data/day8_cost13_payload.json
